WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:02.711
It starts from the beginning.

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:05.004
Nobody told me to win
Wimbledon at 17.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:05.797
I just did it.

00:00:07.298 --> 00:00:09.342
[announcer]
Wimbledon champion, Boris Becker.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.885
My game was power.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.345
Mental strength.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.972
That's how I would describe Boris.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.057
He was like
Michael Jordan in Germany.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.644
Expectations in the tennis world.

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:21.980
Becoming a superstar in sports.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:24.023
You're now a wanted man.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.902
To pick a black woman
as his wife was a big deal.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.988
In the German press it
was a black and white thing.

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:32.615
When you step away
from the game you come into

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:34.033
a completely different life.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.077
It's sort of walking into a dark room.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.830
She came in, she had a big coat on

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.040
and she took the coat off
and she was heavily pregnant.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.000
You just can't believe it.

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:44.878
The wake-up call came very late.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:48.798
[announcer]
Boris Becker is facing two and a half

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:50.717
[announcer]
years in jail for hiding assets

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.885
[announcer]
during bankruptcy.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.511
I've hit my, my bottom.

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.806
That's not the end yet.
There's going to be another chapter.

